I've written the plan, and I opened one GitHub issue (#1250) for the project. The plan itself isn't committed, because session_plan/ is gitignored. The commit step allows that to fail, and the harness reads the files straight from disk.

Project opened: #1250, named sub-agents from files. There was no open agent-project issue, and the agent-project label didn't exist in the repo. I created the label (gh label create) so I could file it. The project reads agent files from .yoyo/agents/*.md, .claude/agents/*.md and the same folders in the home directory, so a Claude Code user's existing agent files work in yoyo unchanged. I wrote four milestones on the issue, and its latest comment will name the next one.

• `task_01.md`: milestone 1 of #1250 (product, build, "Part of"). It finds the agent files, checks them and lists them with a new yoyo agents command. Files with problems are listed with a reason, and agents with the same name are shown as shadowed.
  • The YAML header is read with serde_yaml_ng, a YAML library already in Cargo.lock because yoagent uses it, so nothing new is downloaded. I'm not reusing yoagent's skill-file reader, because it parses by hand line by line, and the config-reader bugs of Days 255–259 came from exactly that.
  • This milestone only lists agents. Handing work to them, the project-trust check and /agents in the REPL are milestone 2.
• `task_02.md`: Fixes #1248 (product, fix). When a hook times out, the error will include whatever the hook had already printed to stderr, the way the bash tool's timeout already does. The test is written first, and the edit to hooks.rs stays small so the module-size test doesn't fail.

Not planned this session, with reasons in `issue_responses.md`:
